Part 1:
1. What is the business problem?
  A grocery store is trying to create a marketing campaign in order to boost sales. This means that the company needs to figure out who 
  they should advertise to in order to maximize profit.  

2. Why is this problem important to the organization?
  This problem is important to the grocery store because if they do not advertise to the right people they will waste money on a 
  marketing. campaign. The hope of the campaign is that it will help the company make more money than they will spend and if they do not
  advertise to the right people they will not meet this goal. Along with this, figuring out who the grocery store should advertise to 
  will allow them to decide how they should advertise to them in order to be the most seen and/or persuasive. 

3. Who is affected by this problem?
  The people affected by this problem is the costumers, this is because they will become subject to the advertisments from the marketing
  campaign whether they specifically want to. 
